Well, the second character ascneded, about a month after my first, and
both after about 6 years of playing.  I must be getting the hang of it.

Miles Teg the Knight was played pretty much like Abomination the
Valkyrie was played;  Lots of running around and bashing things.  The
big thing playing a knight taught me was to be careful while attacking,
and to pay close attention to messages.  This character was also
ascended with somewhat ridiciulous(by my own standards) armor, and once
he started ascending he was never in any real danger.  One of these
days I'll ascend without spending so much time  beefing myelf up- or is
that jus asking for a decent character's death?

The big challenge for this guy was an untimely cursed  BoH.  Even that
turned ok ok, as nothing important vanished when I finally gave up and
looted it.  Thanks everyone with their great advice!   I think knights
have a pretty good deal in this game; I had Excalibur early, a few
timely wishes, and I was decked out in my ascension kit way before I'd
descended to the quest.  This was the first game I'd made use of
Sunsword; As a light source in gehonnom, and as weapon to batter
dischanters with, it served me well, while the +7 grays/+7 saber
handled everything else.  I made good use of the knights skill with
magic as well, though I didn't advance everything.  In fact, once I'l
settled on weapons and spells I plan to use, I pretty much ran out of
things to advance.

I also greatly appreciated riding mounts, at least early, before I had
my own speed. My understanding is that folks can tame and mount many
other fearsome creatures, and jousting can be devastating, but all I
ever did with it was gallop away from a mind flayer at mine's end early
in the game.  I spent almost the entire early game mounted, for the
speed, until I accidentally drowned poor Winter.  And is it me or is
the Magic Mirror of Merlin useless? Especially after the early wish for
GDSM.  Other wishes went for speed boots and a helm of brilliance.  I
had a more or less unused /oW at ascensions- my kit was assembled
early.  The dungeon provided.

Anyway, for my YAFAP, i didn't include any stats because i didn't know
how to dump any. I still don't, but I cut and paste from the final
screen.  Long stuff follows.



